      "documentSlug": "cannabis-and-cannabinoids-in-pd",
      "documentConcept": "Cannabis and cannabinoids in PD",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:372f2c43bdf51a207550bd8add9bb64041d5920c9f770ccdb6cbfc6f76442d94",
      "text": "Systematic reviews and meta-analyses of cannabis and cannabinoids in Parkinson's disease (PD), published 2022 to 2026, report that the evidence does not establish clinical benefit. Individual randomized trials of CBD/THC oils, CBD and nabilone are small and heterogeneous: the Colorado CBD/THC trial and the 2026 S\u00e3o Paulo cannabis-oil trial found no significant difference on their primary outcomes, while one nabilone trial reported a non-motor symptom difference. Reported adverse events include dizziness, confusion and irritability. Positive effects described in uncontrolled studies were not confirmed by small RCTs, per one review. The Parkinson's Foundation does not endorse use for PD symptoms or disease progression. One phase II CBD trial was listed as recruiting in the registry.",
